Note: prime numbers with the sieve of Eratosthenes.

set limit to 100.
set crossed to an empty list.
for every n from 1 to limit, add 0 to crossed.

set primes to an empty list.
for every n from 2 to limit
  if item n of crossed is 0
    add n to primes.
    set multiple to n times n.
    as long as multiple is at most limit
      set item multiple of crossed to 1.
      add n to multiple.
    that's all.
  that's all.
that's all.

say "There are" and then the number of items in primes and then "primes up to" and then limit and then ":".
say primes joined with ", ".
